// Tessera stdlib: the correctly rounded tangent of F16
//
// x splits into x1 + x2 as for sine (cm_f16_trig_split). Then tan(x) = sin(x1 + x2) / cos(x1 + x2), both expanded
// with the addition formulas over F32 values of sin and cos of x1 and x2 from tables tuned so that the F32 quotient
// rounds correctly to F16 everywhere but tiny |x| and seven inputs, handled explicitly. The cos(x2) table is
// sine's (CM_F16_SIN_C2, identical in CORE-MATH). The tables hold NaN for infinite or NaN x. Round to nearest only.
//
// Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binary16/tan/tanf16.c via RazorForge's B16Tan.rf.
// Copyright (c) 2025 Paul Zimmermann
// MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH

module Standard::Core

